From: Codex folio backport <codex@local>
Subject: [PATCH] E404 folio G2.5d: Add filemap_get_folio() (upstream 88/90)

pagecache_get_page() becomes __filemap_get_folio(), and filemap_get_folio()
is a new inline on top of it.  folio_mark_accessed() is added alongside
mark_page_accessed(), which becomes its wrapper.

E404's pagecache_get_page() was simpler than 5.16's, so several upstream
hunks have nothing to convert here:

  - %FGP_HEAD and the find_subpage() call that went with it.  The E404
    xarray holds only head pages, so the entry for @index always starts at
    @index.  There is no FGP_HEAD flag and no find_lock_head() to remove.
  - thp_contains() in the FGP_LOCK truncation check.  The E404 invariant
    was page->index == offset, which becomes folio->index == index.
  - The FGP_WRITE/page_is_idle() branch.  E404's function has no such
    branch; the idle flag is cleared by folio_mark_accessed() instead.
  - FGP_ENTRY.  E404 has no such flag, and its function always turns a
    shadow or swap entry into %NULL, which is kept.

Divergences from upstream, all deliberate:

  - pagecache_get_page() stays a real function in mm/filemap.c rather than
    a static inline, and keeps its EXPORT_SYMBOL.  It is listed in
    android/abi_gki_aarch64_qcom, so the vendor GKI ABI promises the symbol:
    it has to keep existing and keep being exported.  Upstream moves it to
    mm/folio-compat.c, which this tree does not have, and that is where the
    difference would otherwise come from.

  - The wrapper does not consult FGP_HEAD and does not fall back to
    folio_file_page().  Neither exists in this tree, so the head page is
    always the right answer, and the function is three lines instead of the
    eight upstream needs.

  - folio_mark_accessed() keeps E404's body rather than upstream's.  E404
    does not early-return on an unevictable folio and does clear the idle
    flag at the end; upstream's 5.16 body differs on both points, and
    changing either would change behaviour rather than just the type.  The
    compound_head() call is what actually goes away: a folio already is the
    head.

  - mapping_cap_account_dirty() is kept, not mapping_can_writeback().

The G2.5c find_get_entry() wrapper stays: this patch converts
pagecache_get_page() only, and find_lock_entry() plus mm/memcontrol.c still
call it.  Upstream drops it in a later patch once those are converted.

diff --git a/include/linux/pagemap.h b/include/linux/pagemap.h
index 89aafaa..3ac02b1 100644
--- a/include/linux/pagemap.h
+++ b/include/linux/pagemap.h
@@ -314,9 +314,27 @@ pgoff_t page_cache_prev_miss(struct address_space *mapping,
 #define FGP_NOWAIT		0x00000020
 #define FGP_FOR_MMAP		0x00000040
 
+struct folio *__filemap_get_folio(struct address_space *mapping, pgoff_t index,
+		int fgp_flags, gfp_t gfp);
 struct page *pagecache_get_page(struct address_space *mapping, pgoff_t offset,
 		int fgp_flags, gfp_t cache_gfp_mask);
 
+/**
+ * filemap_get_folio - Find and get a folio.
+ * @mapping: The address_space to search.
+ * @index: The page index.
+ *
+ * Looks up the page cache entry at @mapping & @index.  If a folio is
+ * present, it is returned with an increased refcount.
+ *
+ * Otherwise, %NULL is returned.
+ */
+static inline struct folio *filemap_get_folio(struct address_space *mapping,
+					pgoff_t index)
+{
+	return __filemap_get_folio(mapping, index, 0, 0);
+}
+
 /**
  * find_get_page - find and get a page reference
  * @mapping: the address_space to search
